Rules from `[%styled.global]` keep their source order: generate does not
sort them by shorthand depth or by descendant shape. As in plain CSS, the
later `padding: 0` wins on the top side, the later `margin: 10px` wins over
`margin-top: 0`, and the `.foo > div` rule stays where it is written:

  $ cat > global.ml <<EOF
  > [@@@css "h1{padding-top:10px;}"]
  > [@@@css "h1{padding:0;}"]
  > [@@@css ".foo{margin-top:0;}"]
  > [@@@css ".foo > div{color:red;}"]
  > [@@@css ".foo{margin:10px;}"]
  > EOF

  $ styled-ppx.generate global.ml
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  h1{padding-top:10px;}
  h1{padding:0;}
  .foo{margin-top:0;}
  .foo > div{color:red;}
  .foo{margin:10px;}
